    "pr_url": "https://github.com/AMASI-SA/AMASI-SA/pull/1917",
    "pr_body": "## Problem\nThe verified PR1916 release still falls back to the old financial snapshot. A controlled visible attempt completed snapshot loading in9.084s, then source_collection was cancelled after72.943s at the85.040s total deadline. Reconciliation never began. Within collection, recorded_courier_fee repeatedly scans the complete financial history for each eligible order; independent operation counts prove quadratic growth. The live evidence does not establish that this helper alone consumed the entire source phase.\n\n## Change\nBuild one attempt-local fee-history lookup through the existing request-owned preparation worker and use it at both existing fee checks. Preserve complete history, exact prefix/short-circuit/error/Decimal/allocation semantics; unusual structures use the unchanged legacy reader. Rebuild for every collector invocation and CAS retry. Add15 fixed source-substage timing wrappers so any remaining cancellation identifies its actual subphase. No database read, financial mutation, cache across requests, cap increase, deadline extension or authorization change.\n\n## Verification\n-129 new cases pass:116 fee/parity/full-collector/reconciliation/report/lifetime cases and13 timing cases.\n-Root integrated selection:339 passed, actual exit0. Three local Mongo cases were explicitly deselected after connection-refused failures; they remain required without exclusion in exact-A CI's replica set.\n-Independent reviewer:37,386 comparisons against exact J over two hash seeds, comparing values, exception type/message, Decimal flags and input immutability; no blocking finding. Actual visible disconnect joins the worker, releases the owned lease and leaves no nonlease writes or orphan tasks.\n-Negative controls using exact J fail the intended repeated-scan growth assertion. Integrated collector AST matches J after removing only timing wrappers and the intended lookup substitution; old delivery reader remains byte-for-byte unchanged.\n-Paired synthetic timings including full index build:1000/1000 absent-proof0.396461→0.008789s;4000/4000 5.915601→0.030327s;20000 history/250 lookups1.821549→0.056824s. Direct-proof control20000/20000 adds58.6ms (0.007265→0.065864s); no speedup claimed there. Each pair has equal results/unchanged inputs, no DB, actual exit0. These are local observations, not production acceptance.\n\n## Frozen source and pending release\nJ: `9c71435f4a19977c09f4331dee8fddbfa12a45eb`\nA: `8839d3aeb32b4bda2de2015efb0deca7fbb844a3`\nA tree: `492727ceae6b6cada3894e7a450f837186f9a962`\n\nAll source/tests/status are frozen in A. Exact-A CI, official129-case JUnit inclusion in both Operational and Stock, reviewed artifact, intent-only B, normal merge, original-operator build, guarded publish/verify and a fresh visible as_of remain required. Production has not changed by this follow-up. Original /app120 unrelated untracked files and unsaved Untitled-1 remain preserved.\n\n[Source status](https://github.com/AMASI-SA/AMASI-SA/blob/8839d3aeb32b4bda2de2015efb0deca7fbb844a3/docs/operations/OPERATIONAL-SOURCE-COLLECTION-REPAIR-20261114/STATUS.md). Documentation-only continuation branch: `codex/operational-source-collection-handoff-20261114`; never merge or deploy that branch. Issue1006 is at GitHub's2500-comment limit.",
